.TH MKTEMP 3
.SH NAME
mktemp \- make a unique file name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B char *mktemp(char *template);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Mktemp
replaces
.I template
by a unique file name, and returns the
address of the template.
The template should look like a file name with six trailing
X's, which will be replaced with the
current process id and a unique letter.
.PP
.B Note:
it is declared by no header \- v7 had none and C11 has no such routine \- so a
caller declares it itself.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
getpid(2), fopen(3) for
.I tmpnam
.SH FILES
share/besm6/lib/libc.a
.br
lib/libc/gen/mktemp.c
.SH BUGS
.B It walks a single letter,
so it can distinguish 26 names for a given process and no more.  That is why
.IR tmpnam (3)
does
.I not
call it: TMP_MAX promises 26**3, and
.I tmpnam
counts three letters of its own.
